diff --git a/ECTA_R14.tex b/ECTA_R14.tex
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..21c37fb8dc0593d1fe1b2309c7eafd1545317f61
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ECTA_R14.tex
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+\documentclass[ecta]{econsocart}
+\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm,booktabs,tabularx,natbib,microtype}
+\usepackage{hyperref}
+\makeatletter
+\gdef\copyright@text{Revision R14 --- working manuscript}
+\makeatother
+\hypersetup{hidelinks,pdfauthor={Qian QI}}
+\emergencystretch=2em
+\startlocaldefs
+\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}
+\newtheorem{proposition}{Proposition}
+\newtheorem{lemma}{Lemma}
+\newtheorem{assumption}{Assumption}
+\theoremstyle{remark}
+\newtheorem{remark}{Remark}
+\newcommand{\R}{\mathbb R}
+\newcommand{\E}{\mathbb E}
+\newcommand{\cA}{\mathcal A}
+\newcommand{\cR}{\mathcal R}
+\newcommand{\C}{C_\rho}
+\endlocaldefs
+\DeclareFontShape{T1}{ptm}{m}{uc}{<->ssub * ptm/m/sc}{}
+\DeclareFontShape{T1}{ptm}{m}{up}{<->ssub * ptm/m/n}{}
+\DeclareFontShape{T1}{ptm}{m}{scit}{<->ssub * ptm/m/it}{}
+\input{revisions/2026-09-22-r14/paper/result_macros}
+\hypersetup{pdftitle={Neural Bellman Operators -- Revision R14}}
+\begin{document}
+\begin{frontmatter}
+\title{Neural Bellman Operators}
+\runtitle{Neural Bellman Operators}
+\begin{aug}
+\author[id=au1,addressref={add1}]{\fnms{Qian}~\snm{QI}\ead[label=e1]{qiqian@pku.edu.cn}}
+\address[id=add1]{\orgname{Peking University}}
+\end{aug}
+\begin{abstract}
+We study neural policy evaluation and improvement as inputs to constructive verification in stopped continuous-time economies. A whole-domain certificate combines neural derivatives, continuous-action optimization, stopping traces, and feasible-output allowances; a coefficient-transport bound extends the calculation to a class of perturbed models. We execute this certificate on a stored state-feedback actor and critic for an economy with costly preference adjustment. The neural execution is complete, but its current regret bound is not small: the boundary trace exposes an economically important source of error. A separately identified affine-preference dual and feasible policy library provide sharp comparison objects. A second numerical implementation certifies regret below \pricebound\ uniformly over adjustment prices in $[.5,8]$, and below \statebound\ jointly over a nondegenerate initial-state rectangle and those prices. Exact breakpoint calculations distinguish policy accuracy from resolved welfare differences. Full-library perturbation tests, an alternative high-precision decomposition, and newly generated policy-richness experiments make the numerical claims reproducible without treating optimizer convergence or solver superiority as consequences of verification.
+\end{abstract}
+\begin{keyword}
+\kwd{Stochastic control}\kwd{Neural Bellman operators}\kwd{Preference adjustment}\kwd{Validated numerics}\kwd{Policy verification}\kwd{Computational economics}
+\end{keyword}
+\end{frontmatter}
+\input{revisions/2026-09-22-r14/paper/main}
+\begin{appendix}
+\input{revisions/2026-09-22-r14/paper/proofs}
+\end{appendix}
+\input{revisions/2026-09-22-r14/paper/references}
+\end{document}
diff --git a/R14_REVIEW.md b/R14_REVIEW.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..374148acae67fad57087a8613723d55a51f308a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/R14_REVIEW.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Neural Bellman Operators — R14 review entry point
+
+**Current local manuscript:** `ECTA_R14.pdf` / `ECTA_R14.tex`.
+**Current technical supplement:** `SUPP_R14.pdf` / `SUPP_R14.tex`.
+**Response:** `revisions/2026-09-22-r14/response_to_referee.md`.
+**Identities:** `revisions/2026-09-22-r14/canonical_manifest.json` and `publication_receipt.json`.
+
+This is a new data-bearing revision, not the R12 review report under an R13 branch name. Its main paper is 18 pages; its current technical supplement is 11 pages. The old manuscript files remain unchanged.
+
+Read the current residual theorem, the actual full-domain neural error budget, the independently implemented original-economy certificates, the joint state–price construction, and the fresh accuracy/resource experiment. The response maps every R13 finding and the remaining R12 conditions to exact evidence paths.
+
+The neural whole-domain calculation is executed but does not meet the sharp economic tolerance. The tight economic bounds belong to explicitly identified feasible time-control policies and an upper comparison over all adapted controls. Neither those bounds nor the action-only high-dimensional experiment is relabeled as an accurate high-dimensional neural feedback solution.
+
+**Remote status: not published by this session.** GitHub reads and artifact download succeeded; no repository-write action was exposed, and direct Git connection failed DNS resolution. Local reconstructed history, local scientific commits, and original remote review inputs have separate identifiers. A fail-closed helper applies the supplied patch to the exact remote review base without force-pushing or touching old branches.
